From 636ef90aa1ff75ca8731b84b1526e6a557cffcd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dongkyun Son <dongkyun.s@samsung.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:25:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] packaging: split tool subpackages into a standalone
 llvm-tools-subpkgs spec

* 3a5189033a1f - packaging: move tool subpackages to a standalone llvm-tools-subpkgs spec
* d364b338759a - bolt: create ZLIB/LibXml2 targets in standalone build
* 28e72ec6b05d - bolt: mirror X86 mnemonic tables and helpers for standalone build
* 1b9c1ce174de - packaging: add --build-id=sha1 to toolchain linker flags
* 0cc528da035e - bolt: standalone build fixes for LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB=ON
* 3abe328e2c30 - packaging: build profiling tools and BOLT for armv7l (Tizen)
* d3f74e4f484d - packaging: add Obsoletes and python3 Requires to llvm; tidy tools subpackages
* c7edd8f43c66 - packaging: note that scan-build needs clang at runtime
* 67304f964043 - packaging: install with DESTDIR and do not ship libgomp/libiomp5 links

Keep in-tree BOLT on component libraries by setting BOLT_LLVM_LINK_MODE
before its consumers. List the unused X86 mirror in LLVM_OPTIONAL_SOURCES
and compile it only for standalone dylib builds. Clear the inherited
runtime C and C++ flags only for standalone builds.

Restore ARM;BPF as the armv7l LLVM target list and drop the explicit
python3 requirement from llvm. Limit the standalone spec to x86_64 and
aarch64, set BOLT_TARGETS_TO_BUILD per architecture, and verify target
registration.

Bind the LLVM provider build requirements to the LLVM version and check
that the installed providers share one version and release. Keep the
libllvm version requirement for bolt and remove its compiler-rt runtime
requirement. Derive LLVM_LIBDIR_SUFFIX from %{_lib}, retain distribution
LDFLAGS, correct the debug packaging comments, and let CMake install
merge-fdata once.

Change-Id: Ie2c1d45cea6703a0caef72187397275a03e66468
Signed-off-by: Dongkyun Son <dongkyun.s@samsung.com>
Signed-off-by: Pareek Eshaan <e.pareek@samsung.com>
Co-Authored-By: Cline SR
Signed-off-by: Hao Lin <hao.lin@samsung.com>
